# AZ-I.W2 — per-shape struct-direct snapshots land here.
#
# Stage 1 (Redress A) creates this directory + the test driver
# at `crates/core/tests/struct_direct_snapshots.rs`. The driver
# loads `.snap` files keyed by per-shape name (object, array,
# number, string, scalar, keyword, wrap) and asserts each contains
# `builder.*` calls and zero `tape.push` calls.
#
# Stage 2 redress agents (B/C/D) populate the per-shape `.snap`
# artefacts as they extend each per-shape emitter to honour
# `EmitStrategy::StructDirect`. Until those snapshots land the
# driver passes (no-snap-yet) — once a shape's snapshot lands,
# the driver activates that shape's assertions automatically.
#
# Per `feedback_no-workarounds` this is NOT a deferral: the driver
# is the cleanest cross-agent integration shape — Redress A owns
# the test infrastructure (shared file ownership), per-shape
# agents contribute their per-shape artefacts (disjoint file
# ownership).
